d party.\nL50: \nL51: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL52: ### In this section\nL53: \nL54:   * 【15†MPs, Lords & offices home】\nL55:   * 【16†MPs†members.parliament.uk】\nL56:   * 【17†Members of the House of Lords†members.parliament.uk】\nL57:   * 【18†Government & opposition†members.parliament.uk】\nL58:   * 【19†Parliamentary offices】\nL59:   * 【20†Members' allowances】\nL60:   * 【21†Standards and financial interests】\nL61: ### Members of Parliament\nL62: \nL63: 【22†Find your MP Search for Members by name, postcode, or constituency†members.parliament.uk】 【17†Search for Members of the House of Lords Learn about their experience, knowledge and interests.†members.parliament.uk】\nL64: \nL65: ## About Parliament\nL66: \nL67: Parliament examines what the Government is doing, makes new laws, holds the power to set taxes and debates the issues of the day.\nL68: \nL69: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL70: ### In this section\nL71: \nL72:   * 【23†About Parliament home】\nL73:   * 【24†How Parliament works】\nL74:   * 【25†About MPs, Lords & officers】\nL75:   * 【26†Independent Complaints and Grievance Scheme (ICGS)】\nL76:   * 【27†Living Heritage】\nL77:   * 【28†Careers at Parliament】\nL78:   * 【29†Frequently Asked Questions】\nL79:   * 【30†Sustainability and environmental performance in Parliament】\nL80:   * 【31†UK Parliament's Modern Slavery Programme】\nL81: ## Get involved\nL82: \nL83: Read about how to contact an MP or Lord, petition Parliament and find out details of events in your area.\nL84: \nL85: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL86: \nL87: ### In this section\nL88: \nL89:   * 【32†Get involved home】\nL90:   * 【33†Contact an MP or a Member of the Lords】\nL91:   * 【34†Join a learning programme】\nL92:   * 【35†Research impact at the UK Parliament】\nL93:   * 【36†Have your say: Laws and debates】\nL94:   * 【37†Y Gornel Gymraeg】\nL95: ### Get involved with Parliament\nL96: \nL97: 【33†Contact an MP or Lord Contact your MP or a Member of the House of Lords about an issue that matters to you.】 【38†Keep up to date Sign up for the Your Parliament newsletter to find out how you can get involved.†parliament.us16.list-manage.com】\nL98: \nL99: ### It starts with action\nL100: \nL101:   * 【39†Sign or create a petition】\nL102:   * 【40†Sign up to UK Parliament Week†www.ukparliamentweek.org】\nL103: ## Visit Parliament\nL104: \nL105: Find out how to take a tour in person, join an online event, book tickets and plan a visit to UK Parliament.\nL106: \nL107: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL108: \nL109: ### In this section\nL110: \nL111:   * 【41†Visit Parliament home】\nL112:   * 【42†Tours】\nL113:   * 【43†Talks and events】\nL114:   * 【44†Watch debates and committees】\nL115:   * 【45†Plan your visit】\nL116:   * 【46†360° virtual tour】\nL117:   * 【47†Venue hire】\nL118:   * 【3†Parliament Shop†www.shop.parliament.uk】\nL119: ### Keep up to date\nL120: \nL121: 【48†Visit newsletter Sign up to our newsletter to receive the latest news about visiting UK Parliament.†parliament.us14.list-manage.com】\nL122: \nL123: ## Learning\nL124: \nL125: Your UK Parliament offers free, flexible support for teachers, community groups, and home educators to spark engagement and active citizenship.\nL126: \nL127: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL128: ### In this section\nL129: \nL130:   * 【49†Learning home†learning.parliament.uk】\nL131:   * 【50†About UK Parliament education†learning.parliament.uk】\nL132:   * 【51†Teacher resources and lesson plans†learning.parliament.uk】\nL133:   * 【52†CPD Training†learning.parliament.uk】\nL134:   * 【53†Outreach†learning.parliament.uk】\nL135:   * 【54†Visit†learning.parliament.uk】\nL136: ### Supporting teachers\nL137: \nL138: 【54†Inspire your students Book a school visit, classroom workshop or teacher-training session†learning.parliament.uk】 【55†Free teacher training resources Access videos, worksheets, lesson plans and games.†learning.parliament.uk】\nL139: \nL140: ### Keep up to date\nL141: \nL142:   * 【56†Sign up to our education newsletter†parliament.us16.list-manage.com】\nL143: \nL144: ## Shop\nL145: \nL146: Shop\nL147: \nL148: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL149: \nL150: ### In this section\nL151: \nL152:   * 【3†Shop home†www.shop.parliament.uk】\nL153: \nL154: 【57†UK Parliament】\nL155: # Government and Opposition roles\nL156: \nL157: Government ministers and Opposition spokespersons all work in the House of Commons. Specific Peers also represent government departments and opposition parties in the House of Lords.\nL158: ### Prime Minister\nL159: \nL160: The Prime Minister is an MP and head of the government. The leader of the party that wins the most seats in a general election is appointed Prime Minister by the King.\nL161: \nL162: The Prime Minister is officially responsible for choosing the other members of the government.\nL163: \nL164: The Prime Minister can decide when to ask the Monarch to dissolve Parliament and hold a general election.\nL165: The Prime Minister answers questions every Wednesday in the House of Commons from midday to 12.30pm. Questions can come from any MP and on any subject.\nL166: ### Leader of the Opposition\nL167: \nL168: The leader of the largest opposition party is the Leader of the Official Opposition. This role commands an additional salary to the parliamentary salary received as an MP. The Leader of the Official Opposition picks a 'Shadow Cabinet' to follow the work of government departments.\nL169: ### Cabinet\nL170: \nL171: The Cabinet consists of a maximum of twenty-two paid government ministers chosen by the Prime Minister. They can be Members of either House of Parliament. The Cabinet develop government policies and some members head government departments.\nL172: \nL173: ### Shadow Cabinet\nL174: \nL175: The Shadow Cabinet consists of members from the main opposition party in the House of Commons and Lords. Its role is to examine the work of each government department and develop policies in their specific areas.\nL176: ## See also\nL177: \nL178:   * 【58†The Speaker】\nL179:   * 【59†The Lord Speaker】\nL180:   * 【60†Leader of the House of Lords】\nL181: \nL182: ## House of Commons Enquiry Service\nL183: \nL184: If you have a question about the work, history or membership of the House of Commons, contact the Enquiry Service via hcenquiries@parliament.uk\nL185: \nL186: 【61†Find out more】\nL187: \nL188: ## Related information\nL189: ### Useful links\nL190: \nL191:   * 【62†10 Downing Street (Prime Minister)†www.gov.uk】\nL192:   * 【63†Cabinet Office†www.cabinetoffice.gov.uk】\nL193:   * 【64†Labour Party†www.labour.org.uk】\nL194:   * 【65†Conservative Party†www.conservatives.com】\nL195: \nL196: Please note - Parliament is not responsible for the content of external websites.\nL197: \nL198: ### Watch Prime Minister's Questions\nL199: \nL200: 【66†Watch live and archived footage of Prime Minister's Questions †www.youtube.com】\nL201: ###### Popular\nL202: \nL203:   * 【67†What's on in Parliament†whatson.parliament.uk】\nL204:   * 【68†Petitions†petition.parliament.uk】\nL205:   * 【28†Careers at Parliament】\nL206:   * 【69†Commons Media Relations】\nL207:   * 【70†Lords Press Office】\nL208:   * 【71†Contact us】\nL209: \nL210: ###### Research\nL211: \nL212:   * 【72†Commons Library†commonslibrary.parliament.uk】\nL213:   * 【73†Lords Library†lordslibrary.parliament.uk】\nL214:   * 【74†POST†post.parliament.uk】\nL215: \nL216: ###### Search Parliament\nL217: \nL218: [Input]\nL219: \nL220: [Input]\nL221: \nL222: ###### Watch Parliament Live\nL223: \nL224: 【75†Parliament Live TV†parliamentlive.tv】\nL225: ###### Follow Parliament\nL226: \nL227: ###### Legal\nL228: \nL229:   * 【76†Accessibility statement】\nL230:   * 【31†Modern slavery statement】\nL231:   * 【77†About this site】\nL232:   * 【78†Privacy notice】\nL233:   * 【79†Cookie policy】\nL234:   * 【2†Cookie settings】\nL235: \nL236: © UK Parliament 2026\n"
